## sn43.44
sn43.44:1.1 | S: “Mendicants, I will teach you the final haven and the path that leads to the final haven. | T: “Monks, I will also teach you the ultimate and the path leading to the ultimate.
sn43.44:1.2 | S: Listen … | T: Listen & pay close attention. I will speak.”
sn43.44:1.3 | S: And what is the final haven? | T: “As you say, lord,” the monks responded to the Blessed One. The Blessed One said, “Which, monks, is the ultimate?
sn43.44:1.4 | S: The ending of greed, hate, and delusion. | T: Whatever is the ending of passion, the ending of aversion, the ending of delusion:
sn43.44:1.5 | S: This is called the final haven. | T: This is called the ultimate.
sn43.44:1.6 | S: And what is the path that leads to the final haven? | T: “And which is the path leading to the ultimate?
sn43.44:1.7 | S: Mindfulness of the body. | T: Mindfulness immersed in the body:
sn43.44:1.8 | S: This is called the path that leads to the final haven. | T: This is called the path leading to the ultimate.
sn43.44:1.9 | S: So, mendicants, I’ve taught you the final haven and the path that leads to the final haven. | T: Thus, monks, I have taught you the ultimate and the path leading to the ultimate.
sn43.44:1.10 | S: Out of sympathy, I’ve done what a teacher should do who wants what’s best for their disciples. | T: Whatever a sympathetic teacher should do—seeking the welfare of his disciples, out of sympathy for them—that have I done for you.
sn43.44:1.11 | S: Here are these roots of trees, and here are these empty huts. Practice absorption, mendicants! Don’t be negligent! Don’t regret it later! This is my instruction to you.” | T: Over there are the roots of trees; over there, empty dwellings. Practice jhāna, monks. Don’t be heedless. Don’t later fall into remorse. This is our message to you all.”
sn43.44:1.12 | S: (Tell in full as in the unconditioned.) | T: (none)
sn43.44:1.13 | P: Tettiṁsatimaṁ. | T: (none)
sn43.44:1.14 | P: Dutiyo vaggo. | T: (none)
